{"id":"GHSA-5hj8-q7fv-qrj6","axis":"advisories","repo":"russellhaering/gosaml2","sha":"b2bd784b196b21f606faaa6a4eeae929bd75aa20","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"types/encrypted_assertion.go","lines":["@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ func (ea *EncryptedAssertion) DecryptBytes(cert *tls.Certificate) ([]byte, error"," \t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cannot create AES-GCM: %s\", err)"," \t\t}"," ","+\t\tif len(data) < c.NonceSize() {","+\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"encrypted data is smaller than the AES-GCM nonce size %d: actual size %d\", c.NonceSize(), len(data))","+\t\t}"," \t\tnonce, data := data[:c.NonceSize()], data[c.NonceSize():]"," \t\tplainText, err := c.Open(nil, nonce, data, nil)"," \t\tif err != nil {","@@ -66,6 +69,9 @@ func (ea *EncryptedAssertion) DecryptBytes(cert *tls.Certificate) ([]byte, error"," \t\tif len(data)%k.BlockSize() != 0 {"," \t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"encrypted data is not a multiple of the expected CBC block size %d: actual size %d\", k.BlockSize(), len(data))"," \t\t}","+\t\tif len(data) < k.BlockSize() {","+\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"encrypted data is smaller than the expected CBC block size %d: actual size %d\", k.BlockSize(), len(data))","+\t\t}"," \t\tnonce, data := data[:k.BlockSize()], data[k.BlockSize():]"," \t\tc := cipher.NewCBCDecrypter(k, nonce)"," \t\tc.CryptBlocks(data, data)"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"types/encrypted_assertion_test.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@","+// Copyright 2016 Russell Haering et al.","+//","+// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");","+// you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.","+// You may obtain a copy of the License at","+//","+//     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+//","+// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software","+// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,","+// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.","+// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and","+// limitations under the License.","+","+package types","+","+import (","+\t\"crypto/rand\"","+\t\"crypto/rsa\"","+\t\"crypto/sha1\"","+\t\"crypto/tls\"","+\t\"crypto/x509\"","+\t\"crypto/x509/pkix\"","+\t\"encoding/base64\"","+\t\"math/big\"","+\t\"testing\"","+\t\"time\"","+)","+","+func newTestTLSCert(t *testing.T) *tls.Certificate {","+\tt.Helper()","+","+\tpriv, err := rsa.GenerateKey(rand.Reader, 2048)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"generating RSA key: %s\", err)","+\t}","+","+\ttemplate := &x509.Certificate{","+\t\tSerialNumber: big.NewInt(1),","+\t\tSubject:      pkix.Name{CommonName: \"gosaml2 test\"},","+\t\tNotBefore:    time.Now().Add(-time.Hour),","+\t\tNotAfter:     time.Now().Add(time.Hour),","+\t}","+","+\tder, err := x509.CreateCertificate(rand.Reader, template, template, &priv.PublicKey, priv)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"creating certificate: %s\", err)","+\t}","+","+\treturn &tls.Certificate{","+\t\tCertificate: [][]byte{der},","+\t\tPrivateKey:  priv,","+\t}","+}","+","+// newTestEncryptedAssertion builds an EncryptedAssertion whose EncryptedKey","+// decrypts successfully against cert, so that DecryptBytes reaches the","+// symmetric decryption branch under test with cipherValue as the raw","+// (not base64-encoded) EncryptedData CipherValue.","+func newTestEncryptedAssertion(t *testing.T, cert *tls.Certificate, algorithm string, cipherValue []byte) *EncryptedAssertion {","+\tt.Helper()","+","+\tpub := cert.PrivateKey.(*rsa.PrivateKey).Public().(*rsa.PublicKey)","+","+\taesKey := make([]byte, 16)","+\tif _, err := rand.Read(aesKey); err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"generating AES key: %s\", err)","+\t}","+","+\twrappedKey, err := rsa.EncryptOAEP(sha1.New(), rand.Reader, pub, aesKey, nil)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"wrapping AES key: %s\", err)","+\t}","+","+\treturn &EncryptedAssertion{","+\t\tEncryptionMethod: EncryptionMethod{Algorithm: algorithm},","+\t\tEncryptedKey: EncryptedKey{","+\t\t\tCipherValue:      base64.StdEncoding.EncodeToString(wrappedKey),","+\t\t\tEncryptionMethod: EncryptionMethod{Algorithm: MethodRSAOAEP},","+\t\t},","+\t\tCipherValue: base64.StdEncoding.EncodeToString(cipherValue),","+\t}","+}","+","+func TestDecryptBytesShortCipherTextDoesNotPanic(t *testing.T) {","+\tcert := newTestTLSCert(t)","+","+\ttests := []struct {","+\t\tname        string","+\t\talgorithm   string","+\t\tcipherValue []byte","+\t}{","+\t\t{\"GCM empty\", MethodAES128GCM, []byte{}},","+\t\t{\"GCM shorter than nonce\", MethodAES128GCM, []byte{0x01, 0x02, 0x03}},","+\t\t{\"CBC empty\", MethodAES128CBC, []byte{}},","+\t\t{\"CBC shorter than block size\", MethodAES128CBC, []byte{0x01, 0x02, 0x03}},","+\t}","+","+\tfor _, tt := range tests {","+\t\tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tea := newTestEncryptedAssertion(t, cert, tt.algorithm, tt.cipherValue)","+","+\t\t\tdefer func() {","+\t\t\t\tif r := recover(); r != nil {","+\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecryptBytes panicked: %v\", r)","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t}()","+","+\t\t\t_, err := ea.DecryptBytes(cert)","+\t\t\tif err == nil {","+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"expected an error, got nil\")","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}",""],"additions":115,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":121,"deletions":0,"truncated":false,"file_count":2},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-20T17:57:09.559349+00:00"}